{{!-- ignition: noblock --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{{> site/head}}
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<div class="sheet">
{{> site/header}}
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="about sheet-inner">
  <section class="plate" data-plate="01 · manifesto">
    <p class="kicker">about the platform</p>
    <h1>{{title}}</h1>
    <p class="lead"><strong>Kodavr</strong> is a registry of raw experience — "dumps" — with a machine-readable contract, open to any field: engineering, design, finance, construction, sales, and everything in between. Authors publish dumps without polishing; readers' agents adapt them to their own context.</p>
    {{!-- §7.10/KDV-COPY-08: the "what is a dump" story — the demo's left-ruled
         statement block. The prompt stays a copydeck expression (verbatim §7.10). --}}
    <blockquote class="block-statement">
      <p>{{what_is_a_dump.definition}} {{what_is_a_dump.lead}} <span class="dump-prompt">"{{what_is_a_dump.prompt}}"</span> {{what_is_a_dump.tail}}</p>
    </blockquote>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>Dumps are raw: no polishing, no tailoring to an audience.</li>
      <li>The contract is machine-readable, the source is open.</li>
      <li>Readers meet dumps through their own agent, not through the platform — and the agent picks which dumps are worth its user's attention.</li>
    </ul>
    <blockquote class="block-statement emph">
      <p>So publish without fear: your dump does not have to find its reader on its own. The agent selects what is interesting for its particular user, and then rewrites the dump for that user — longer or shorter, in this or another style, with explanations or without. Your raw text becomes exactly what the reader needs; both the selection and the adaptation happen on their side.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <div class="mark-lg"><img src="/logo.svg" alt="Kodavr" width="64" height="64"></div>
    <p class="slogan">{{copy.brand_slogan_lead}}</p>
    <p class="slogan-muted">{{copy.brand_slogans_muted}}</p>
    <p class="micro"><a href="/docs/decisions.md">Architecture decisions</a></p>
  </section>
</main>
{{> site/footer}}
</div>
</body>
</html>
